# APIs & URLs

- Folders under `apis/` mirror URL segments. Classes: `{Entity}ListCreate` / `RetrieveUpdateDestroy`; actions → `*ApiView`.
- Mount via `urls/<prefix>_url.py`; plural resource nouns.
{%- if cookiecutter.use_uuid_pk == "y" %}
- Path ids: `<uuid:entity_id>`.
{%- else %}
- Path ids: `<int:entity_id>`.
{%- endif %}
- Always `api_response` / pagination helpers. Public → `AllowAny`.
- OpenAPI: `envelope_serializer(...)`; document FilterSet query params on filtered lists.
{%- if cookiecutter.use_scoped_apis == "y" %}

## Scoped `/api/v1/<scope>/…`

Scopes: `{{ cookiecutter.api_scopes }}`.

- Domain mounts only under a scope (`api/<scope>_urls.py`). Do not add product routes at bare `/api/v1/`.
- New resources: prefer `apis/<scope>/<resource>/` with `<Scope>*` serializers (see `scoped-apis` rule).
- Scope user tables: `users/models/<scope>_user.py` subclasses `BaseUser` (empty by default).
- Gate with `IsScopeMember` (`request.api_scope`). Add scopes with `add_api_scope`.
{%- endif %}
- Changing URL/layout conventions → update **this rule file** in the **same** change.

